{
  "request": "parental consent form for our primary school to give a pupil medicine during the school day",
  "title": "Consent for the school to give medicine",
  "description": "Use when a parent asks the school to give their child medicine during the school day: the child, the medicine and how to give it, how long for, contacts in an emergency, and the parent's consent.",
  "maxPages": 2,
  "content": {
    "schemaVersion": 3,
    "branding": {
      "organizationName": "",
      "logoAsset": null,
      "logoDataUrl": null,
      "logoAlignment": "left",
      "logoWidthPercent": 24,
      "primaryColor": "#3d2c5e",
      "accentColor": "#6c4f9e"
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "0b130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Consent for the school to give medicine",
        "level": 1,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The school can give your child medicine only when you have filled in and signed this form. Please use one form for each medicine.",
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Before you send the medicine: bring it to the school office yourself, in its original container with the pharmacy label, which must show your child's name, the dose and how often to give it. We cannot accept medicine that is out of date or has been put in another container. The only exception is insulin, which may come in a pen or pump rather than its original container.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "Before you send the medicine:",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " bring it to the school office yourself, in its original container with the pharmacy label, which must show your child's name, the dose and how often to give it. We cannot accept medicine that is out of date or has been put in another container. The only exception is insulin, which may come in a pen or pump rather than its original container."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "How we use your information: we use this form to give your child their medicine safely and to keep a record of each dose. We share it only with the staff who give the medicine or care for your child, and with emergency services if your child needs urgent help. We keep it on your child's school record.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "How we use your information:",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " we use this form to give your child their medicine safely and to keep a record of each dose. We share it only with the staff who give the medicine or care for your child, and with emergency services if your child needs urgent help. We keep it on your child's school record."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
